From: Michele Salerno <mikysal78@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mwlwifi: allow 802.11s mesh point on 88W8964

Mesh support was added and verified only on 88W8997 (commit 9271457) and
add_interface returns -EPERM for every other chip, although
interface_modes advertises NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT unconditionally.
Beacons and mesh IEs are already handled by the common AP code path, so
let 88W8964 (WRT3200ACM/WRT32X) try it.

EXPERIMENTAL: 88W8964 uses the NDP data path, where the firmware rebuilds
the 802.11 header of data frames; mesh data frames may not be handled.

--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -190,7 +190,8 @@ static int mwl_mac80211_add_interface(st
 	case NL80211_IFTYPE_AP:
 	case NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT:
 		if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT)
-			if (priv->chip_type != MWL8997)
+			if (priv->chip_type != MWL8997 &&
+			    priv->chip_type != MWL8964)
 				return -EPERM;
 		macids_supported = priv->ap_macids_supported;
 		break;
